0 Six small pulley arrangements show rubber bands running straight, crossing, turning around idlers and wrapping a single wheel.
0 Name: RUBBER_BAND-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Willy Tschager
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: Several triangular loops use one large wheel and smaller guides. A blue loop crosses itself, a brown loop reaches a tiny motor pulley, and a dark ring hugs one isolated wheel.
0 // Rigid construction: Wedge-belt wheels, bushes and small guides define the routes. One assembly pairs the 2986c01 micromotor with its 2983 pulley and a larger 3736 pulley wheel.
0 // Build lesson: Study shaft spacing, pulley planes and the distinction between a driven wheel and a guide; a visible belt route can explain a machine at a glance.
0 // Reuse: These rigs lack complete bearing frames. The motor-side legacy case warns about an unsolvable tangent in the current synthesizer; do not copy every displayed loop as a valid belt drive.
0 // Study 1: The tan triangular route wraps a large wheel and two small guides, with crossings specified in the source.
